swer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435856} :answer-field/id #uuid "3037a011-e9f1-5dab-aa7d-6ffe3d4faaec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085509} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03f76b8-d043-505d-8492-b243b8108a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085516} {:answer/id #uuid "8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435843} {:answer/id #uuid "ae550e0c-1776-5b97-ab81-e46cb204df85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435850} {:answer/id #uuid "fc50ddf9-0597-5079-a434-4f4d589089a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435843} :answer-field/id #uuid "af75cec9-5a94-548e-88fa-c37d26f071ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8d9c75e9-1ee8-5d41-904e-f9bb375cf039" :question/math-academy-id "q-335808" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot y=x,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =\\int 2{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =2{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =2{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/4} \\\\ 1 & =2+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "117ed42d-e3b1-523b-8f69-150942e554cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308872} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7fd74c-8a73-54ba-b5f8-00d9b9214cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310020} {:answer/id #uuid "e85590a8-371b-51ed-9363-5ee1c845dfb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310594} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ce5eb-4f47-5650-a379-9985a81218f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ce5eb-4f47-5650-a379-9985a81218f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310621} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f85c8ef-b569-567a-8797-508841891ad6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dac0063-ecc2-5627-bb27-eec391f6c6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309090} {:answer/id #uuid "81429b38-817c-58d8-ba84-9a927f701049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} {:answer/id #uuid "cadb2780-5df9-5f0a-9927-a1da1d6dd3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310373} {:answer/id #uuid "d4679384-5633-50c0-98ce-64a2bd94c291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81429b38-817c-58d8-ba84-9a927f701049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} :answer-field/id #uuid "f955a4ed-77cc-558d-8e88-a71d0a0707d4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7bd80c89-2759-5cf8-8ba7-8fb4c49482e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-335810" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The first step is to write the equation in standard form,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,.\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y & =4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 4x \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={1}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{1}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =1+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11d5a1d-e93d-5a5d-8111-e33d997e2841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(ye^{x}) = e^{x} \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087270} {:answer/id #uuid "e572ebc9-141f-578b-93ec-080a0deeb913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y \\cdot 2x) = 2x \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087271} {:answer/id #uuid "fd667700-3e8d-53d0-9c71-264753a1f8cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx^{2}) = x^{2} \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087272} {:answer/id #uuid "6e285ba0-0b5f-5e5a-a7bd-e5b3de551a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(ye^{x^{2}}) = e^{x^{2}} \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087273} {:answer/id #uuid "76e91a95-c637-5848-86e4-e944f3eee17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx) = x \\cdot 2xe^{-x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087274}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8fe340-5770-5791-befc-e802db4415ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087269}] :question/id #uuid "8973fb88-5098-5e4b-a0b0-25638565dd93" :question/math-academy-id "q-8546" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2xy = 2xe^{-x^{2}}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e163d8-4a78-504d-8269-402a0415e08e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2x)=2x\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281750} {:answer/id #uuid "4382d319-73fb-5cb1-9dfc-25d3c057b161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282265} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff9a224-fab5-5e91-b0ff-979e6a4e2c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2)=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282648} {:answer/id #uuid "bae778d3-7532-5194-9c25-d299082a3153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{2x})={e}^{2x}\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283301} {:answer/id #uuid "c179d6ec-3d07-5033-ad1d-7ca1e0d4284e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4382d319-73fb-5cb1-9dfc-25d3c057b161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282265} :answer-field/id #uuid "4288ef37-6c06-5c5f-a10c-1e0e96591b46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "65a9092a-d6a6-5192-82ca-c04151a6438f" :question/math-academy-id "q-17533" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{e}^{x}y & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217ccf45-8734-56ec-b06d-0fa3666f9d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281985} {:answer/id #uuid "610a3a60-2d25-5e70-9070-a40fd0b17bcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282515} {:answer/id #uuid "692ebc86-2eeb-51e8-909d-911b7bbb78b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282591} {:answer/id #uuid "887e5de7-cd20-589e-9062-1ed36efe796c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x})={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282865} {:answer/id #uuid "99833182-f1d2-5cc1-b043-ddfe57635bc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "692ebc86-2eeb-51e8-909d-911b7bbb78b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282591} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd94faa5-6de0-52b0-a454-db6562b0e660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0dcacbda-1dc5-5146-b0bc-75c7bab3748d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17539" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y) & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+y & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(yx) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e2b089-092a-5eca-9f7e-bf626ffedb03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2})={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309516} {:answer/id #uuid "71425229-5e0c-56e4-a3c5-6da6bfb56a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x/2})={e}^{x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309627} {:answer/id #uuid "cd378351-ace0-5392-8e0c-b064ad6a0d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{x}{2}\\right))=-\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310393} {:answer/id #uuid "e71cd363-dab5-57e2-b1a7-f9cdab639247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right))=-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310584} {:answer/id #uuid "f08a16be-ff29-5897-9836-28db90a5052f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2)=2{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e2b089-092a-5eca-9f7e-bf626ffedb03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2})={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309516} :answer-field/id #uuid "b03a098b-971d-55f6-a30b-4a30fe70ddf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dba525fe-7e4d-5319-88bd-1b806feb0904" :question/math-academy-id "q-335278" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{2}y={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $Q(x)={x}^{3}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1/2)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{2}y) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2}) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a488da-8074-50a9-ba1d-c7e0f32bf719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308780} {:answer/id #uuid "64a5c638-4dbb-57eb-a6fb-248e76429030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309522} {:answer/id #uuid "893e7fae-64e2-57b6-af19-e61e904ea8b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309829} {:answer/id #uuid "9e515d8a-f8c4-5ea9-9b59-674573d38b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310026} {:answer/id #uuid "b92c0b6e-441f-5b77-9aa7-a8dc52625f53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a488da-8074-50a9-ba1d-c7e0f32bf719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308780} :answer-field/id #uuid "785b77fb-6634-5289-8f5e-c7972e2ca683" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223e604f-882b-578c-9005-65a6a468f7c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309006} {:answer/id #uuid "3a151fdc-c615-56f8-af30-2dacf342942e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309195} {:answer/id #uuid "7b511ce9-9c0e-54e8-8e7e-93916e342c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711} {:answer/id #uuid "ad26b27d-2be0-5935-829c-fe759d649c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b511ce9-9c0e-54e8-8e7e-93916e342c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c99e1a2-52bb-5b04-85f5-ed344de385bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d36870f2-83c3-53eb-b9c4-cfdc50550717" :question/math-academy-id "q-335409" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c590c3-891b-511b-9e8d-1e0317eac036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309024} {:answer/id #uuid "c4250262-bc93-5a7e-a34a-2623ae9d7561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310322} {:answer/id #uuid "c82f0da4-6a92-5001-89a2-66f34618a0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310355} {:answer/id #uuid "ee20a83a-6373-5864-bf59-eeaad3c5fb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4250262-bc93-5a7e-a34a-2623ae9d7561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310322} :answer-field/id #uuid "26833fad-1674-5264-a99a-1ab167ee5815" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e87914-2491-5ea9-986c-2fa933b9f42e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} {:answer/id #uuid "93802e8a-2438-526b-9013-756c85306841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309928} {:answer/id #uuid "cc68d1a8-cb75-5053-8d7d-c7bbccf33bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310385} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5f5849-731e-572b-9350-7951b8593415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e87914-2491-5ea9-986c-2fa933b9f42e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} :answer-field/id #uuid "842dfce6-3596-5e08-aa3d-f4ed3e02c6ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "039312c7-7497-5736-bf10-d497d1c61328" :question/math-academy-id "q-335412" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{3})\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2217ec13-aeca-54c6-b184-b9c6f12eca21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309005} {:answer/id #uuid "278ab869-b3ab-5209-b251-49e30ed08f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309045} {:answer/id #uuid "cb884bde-aa7d-5ea3-8269-75c1c85782d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378} {:answer/id #uuid "e304072c-14d0-5b9a-91ef-e7c21ca3967c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb884bde-aa7d-5ea3-8269-75c1c85782d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d4b8151-a2dd-5d21-b3a8-5f1786ce72f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51d8ba46-b7ec-5aeb-9c2e-92c427b44105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309368} {:answer/id #uuid "6e835f28-6c17-5099-9e1d-5557f103db76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309601} {:answer/id #uuid "784a4e7f-4997-59d7-9dbf-2d44fdbb9535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309692} {:answer/id #uuid "88322c85-406a-50de-beb7-e95ff2a7c6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309817} {:answer/id #uuid "f316da64-a8b2-5ef5-a90e-929545648a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "784a4e7f-4997-59d7-9dbf-2d44fdbb9535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309692} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edac9dd-3740-53a2-adc8-4f1b9b142575" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eb60ed14-2886-5407-9edd-93c36aa77da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335811" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2y}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},\\,y(\\pi )=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\pi )=0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48e70df3-e69a-52ce-adaf-9d80576fc124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309306} {:answer/id #uuid "4de60ca3-08eb-5908-84e7-337d050635cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309339} {:answer/id #uuid "60127d29-07b2-5438-b25c-538c97234290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309472} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e91b0c-4363-5464-927a-584f15d25ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310236} {:answer/id #uuid "e373d4bf-5114-5201-a0ca-5837cf70ed2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7e91b0c-4363-5464-927a-584f15d25ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310236} :answer-field/id #uuid "964f9aee-69e3-5eaf-ba62-46327eb55e3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd4c10d-4104-533e-a7ea-701ca41dc419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309354} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab118d1-7dd3-5f85-b172-3299a04f369d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309705} {:answer/id #uuid "976ecd48-d13c-560a-802a-8e7cf948da05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309962} {:answer/id #uuid "de8dc48e-6d1c-5472-ac5b-8b94b9419130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "976ecd48-d13c-560a-802a-8e7cf948da05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309962} :answer-field/id #uuid "fba4b49a-a123-5ea4-a04f-61aaf7f9c4c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3bbe03fd-0d2c-564c-9b93-a7997b3f7696" :question/math-academy-id "q-335812" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0,\\,y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ yx & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+C}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2C}{\\pi } \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a701b78-2f7b-5869-a35c-a68265d84c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312297} {:answer/id #uuid "35b399dd-b281-56b7-8db7-a76855d06ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312408} {:answer/id #uuid "c01117c8-2cdb-582a-8d44-4d6c98807eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313480} {:answer/id #uuid "e4465b0a-93ed-52f4-b50c-bf89f91e8717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4465b0a-93ed-52f4-b50c-bf89f91e8717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313777} :answer-field/id #uuid "619b5a02-9bcf-5c4e-9804-90020e919aba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8ab38f-ccc9-5c4d-9953-e2511696a304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312314} {:answer/id #uuid "82438980-e317-5426-8c57-7d992347312f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313024} {:answer/id #uuid "a83c841e-df51-5c6e-b081-e26fb120e44e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313294} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3cf1a5-b0c2-595f-a092-5ea9a23fd911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82438980-e317-5426-8c57-7d992347312f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313024} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5afcbd6-0c6a-5f61-91f9-74372beb0557" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f406ffe6-dbd4-575f-96ea-c90a9a6d9f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-339140" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y=7,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{5}{x}$ and $Q(x)=7.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (5/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5})} \\\\  & ={x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{5}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y) & ={x}^{5}\\cdot 7 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{x}^{4}y & =7{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{5})\\,dx & =\\int 7{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "205e27b5-4aef-53eb-8cf0-e7365d5f4c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345637} {:answer/id #uuid "7510063a-6cf7-5663-bf6a-5afc7e2ed0eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346382} {:answer/id #uuid "8483449c-5ecd-5c41-92e1-0ded8b81ec2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-x})={e}^{-x}{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346505} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c267a8-32e4-55c8-8af3-388216c0c46a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346964} {:answer/id #uuid "cf856d8b-bb28-5fc8-bf77-c77ea36fa1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9c267a8-32e4-55c8-8af3-388216c0c46a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346964} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b3a3107-9d3a-5db2-9a74-94dd3b070895" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7613e649-714b-58e4-9ccc-7a0b944dc47c" :question/math-academy-id "q-79818" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y={e}^{x},\\,x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)={e}^{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y) & =x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cf29a8-7002-55ea-90d8-6e36bd328018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346547} {:answer/id #uuid "bbbc1949-1dc3-5132-b9a6-2f5a02db8b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346980} {:answer/id #uuid "c06aae51-d699-5f08-973e-040bd676bd09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347016} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fb694c-f9b1-5dce-86ee-87c1b3194d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347181} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d204d7-b947-5d35-bd31-8a40d4cc447b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot 2)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbbc1949-1dc3-5132-b9a6-2f5a02db8b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346980} :answer-field/id #uuid "b92de6c6-2fc5-5d10-b5ab-f609af76b489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2870a84c-606f-5fc5-a1ed-a94d670c16ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-79819" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=1\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd0b65e-3a0f-5994-9689-9aef5b5c9454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{-x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391570} {:answer/id #uuid "3fae5784-6514-5371-820c-1909539d4c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391571} {:answer/id #uuid "58c34fda-7cad-508d-a7f2-d8bf06c08b7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391572} {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573} :answer-field/id #uuid "d308949f-707a-5a2c-802c-a0a17c33433a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4e6cf3c-fccb-5029-b604-d1593b0daddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391575} {:answer/id #uuid "1e61f74a-48e8-542c-a33f-c9fe7a376f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391576} {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} {:answer/id #uuid "fb69fbee-2b0a-5d6f-b11d-267cf756dd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} :answer-field/id #uuid "2021aa17-0151-5e2d-987a-a1856edc5e53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6530e5db-b521-5f5c-99f7-59872d852e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-335402" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=6{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is already in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=6{e}^{2x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot 6{e}^{2x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =6{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =6{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =-6{e}^{-x}+C \\\\ y & =-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb9195b-384d-5b2f-bad0-6dd43e0f4b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391595} {:answer/id #uuid "f34ac63a-04a2-52a7-a90f-f8f4d8d09299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391596} {:answer/id #uuid "2d29d24c-fd03-58f5-91b9-3629bcaeee91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391597} {:answer/id #uuid "f585add5-def6-5238-932b-3a30184083f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391598} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599} :answer-field/id #uuid "7806b0bb-9404-54a9-9afe-9fe5aae500c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} {:answer/id #uuid "185130ca-9e63-5f95-8858-fbe1360a02af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391602} {:answer/id #uuid "24752170-0362-5a79-8550-d496d2deb223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391603} {:answer/id #uuid "7644849e-bdfd-532f-b35d-2dd327bd7b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5f76ae-1afb-592e-a102-26dd10e20b42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c6ef87c-1a0b-5973-8a1d-74f719874948" :question/math-academy-id "q-335806" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x{e}^{-x},\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2x{e}^{-x}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 2x{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x}) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{x} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ y & =({x}^{2}+C){e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =({0}^{2}+C){e}^{-0} \\\\ -2 & =(0+C)\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc0fd51-b3d5-5b60-822b-55ce1a39a048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391608} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5f9c6d-a3bd-55c8-a595-021440af2d20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-5{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391609} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff86545-6fe9-59ce-a43b-d596ae985d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391610} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e86c18-962f-5498-8cd8-fd15eaf09b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c53fba-addc-5347-89bc-46926b4cec8a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68eff5b7-73e9-589d-b262-8718bbf64cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391613} {:answer/id #uuid "708406f2-8554-5163-8a8c-780da5f0a24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391614} {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} {:answer/id #uuid "878ffcb1-ce95-5b25-bcf5-982716631d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0dfecd2-1e22-5e5a-aff3-e35469e93c9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cba95378-fbb4-59fe-bb7c-3f501d3e7ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335829" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{4x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ {e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{4x}\\cdot y & =8{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x}) & =8{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =8(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x})+C \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =2{e}^{4x}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-4(0)} \\\\ -1 & =2+C(1) \\\\ C & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-3{e}^{-4x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5e5efa-0ad9-5cb1-8007-def75d4c0f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391733} {:answer/id #uuid "181ce215-60ee-5a98-8d16-1f87a5c66bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391734} {:answer/id #uuid "c201762a-3b3f-52e3-a4c2-6f449ab4bd0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391735} {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52979ca-88b2-53be-b424-0a20f99bf0c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02bcb740-d3b0-5e03-ac52-deeb78de3ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391738} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0496f9-803e-5f66-af97-d84ac1ef5ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391739} {:answer/id #uuid "917a7312-27b6-560b-80be-1afb23076cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391740} {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e39085e-c8a9-5cbc-b6d2-646a14b27243" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "08d92346-a7e8-58c6-8d60-e4702d743dd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-339138" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{3x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot x{e}^{3x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c73a7b2-a2bf-518a-beb1-31fbbadf0c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397298} {:answer/id #uuid "d70f278f-f71b-563b-90a5-a72e4490f97d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397299} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9aa96a-e438-54ed-91f2-a9cd9b89c2af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397300} {:answer/id #uuid "be7b681a-d4b7-5605-ba2e-22acaaed6363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397301} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c6d291-cf90-51ae-b2e3-e5400146213f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e829349-3bd7-53b1-81eb-45b5da9870a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{12x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397304} {:answer/id #uuid "ddaeb121-e0a6-501b-9a51-af6c7d17b5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397305} {:answer/id #uuid "831b7918-1f4b-50de-b1bd-28a0091624cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397306} {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cc20f5-acca-5b79-8f90-bd4ac033d4c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435836} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb32a9a-ce7c-5dfe-90c1-5f241762ceee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435842} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf9a5e7-9387-5f18-9a2c-3d8174e2d646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435852} {:answer/id #uuid "f669873b-95d4-589e-957f-2bb522268738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435836} :answer-field/id #uuid "054a463e-8111-5ef5-af3f-4d0babd67edf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435840} {:answer/id #uuid "96612919-8760-51a3-a0ec-f59a5ea738c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435844} {:answer/id #uuid "a91ab2dc-5a5e-503c-8f55-0ebae59165d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435848} {:answer/id #uuid "cceac854-6bb0-51ac-8a27-c1be3b7727f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435840} :answer-field/id #uuid "658b2e4e-a8cb-5de8-9ced-3ee2b6b96997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339139" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=5.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot 5 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}y & =5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & ={x}^{5}+C \\\\ y & =x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b978ec0-c1dc-593e-85ec-c512eb8b8bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x|)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435832} {:answer/id #uuid "1da376ec-fadc-58b2-9050-98c3a0e3289d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435835} {:answer/id #uuid "39544074-ae02-530d-9e3a-2a0b0340a99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{2x})={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435838} {:answer/id #uuid "97ed5649-7d28-5597-8785-b502fbbd5161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2x)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435845} {:answer/id #uuid "a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}})={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6707d7d-a941-50a8-9de7-4cedeafd40fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}})={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435847} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf5e5ce-2a24-563a-8eed-d37940cab8bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "73fd6309-052f-5dd1-8e4c-82525a25d454" :question/math-academy-id "q-335274" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=2x$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2x\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}}) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d921686-f16a-5dba-8a57-bf18cea65de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}(1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435834} {:answer/id #uuid "21b21254-3e18-5695-9053-f6ca9ce7117b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-2x}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435837} {:answer/id #uuid "ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435849} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7b3997-dd21-54f1-8bae-4ea74ec54405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(3+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435854} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b016d8-b939-5406-bcfa-caab3f97d6bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435849} :answer-field/id #uuid "872a01bb-a58c-517b-8a38-5d170114d390" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435831} {:answer/id #uuid "12775c73-4492-5f55-9c3e-64f7ff76cc43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435833} {:answer/id #uuid "89b946b2-2ff0-52e9-9809-36bbebc85401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435841} {:answer/id #uuid "b2373707-12f6-5094-9104-60d956b3f32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435831} :answer-field/id #uuid "db6d7e71-81cf-5a3b-b7fa-5481d846b976" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eb095d57-a547-5e39-b061-eaeaefb98858" :question/math-academy-id "q-335830" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-2x} & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & ={e}^{2x}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={e}^{2(0)}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\ 4 & =C-1 \\\\ C & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9883db31-c965-5a25-a3db-2fe7202d1718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495347} {:answer/id #uuid "acd0d970-3e90-555a-961f-735eefa2db11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495353} {:answer/id #uuid "cdff44bf-d414-52e1-adf1-e4edbb9765ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495361} {:answer/id #uuid "f28fc0f9-3e8d-5e9f-b499-4bccbcb13076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{6 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495369} {:answer/id #uuid "fee4d65e-8697-59f0-8f1d-ea6283a9d22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdff44bf-d414-52e1-adf1-e4edbb9765ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495361} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b5c6eb-3118-5eb5-9108-444148635772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "03f01512-4546-59df-8e70-3aa004e3020a" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3 x\\right)\\cdot y=x^{4}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor.\n\nAssume $x>0$." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y=x^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3$ and $Q(x)=x^{3}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(3\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223242e6-657c-5bec-8429-628abde472df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495317} {:answer/id #uuid "2616a25d-dc53-5253-a481-88bfdb77dd30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495319} {:answer/id #uuid "2824925e-5b26-5a3d-ac14-d9fecafbcf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495320} {:answer/id #uuid "91e8878f-4919-5880-ad79-fe8271c9a55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495345} {:answer/id #uuid "b97d76c6-b915-54b0-bcf7-c2824c4dd262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2824925e-5b26-5a3d-ac14-d9fecafbcf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495320} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d3a783d-5c90-57dd-b22c-25811200de97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1fa0b599-1031-5002-a477-8a20611908f9" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-1$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(-1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52024f4a-ebc0-5103-a1e8-78758bc1c99d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{4 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{4 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495327} {:answer/id #uuid "74506bb6-4469-5ca5-9318-2f49b6ac1c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495336} {:answer/id #uuid "7d011e5a-cc83-508a-8044-57460dbf