cd-59b7-891e-bbbed0f81ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495378} :answer-field/id #uuid "c09f627b-2b26-5a25-a69f-2ebc31d491f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0f568c95-a616-5b36-b27c-7ed5df478cdc" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)y=\\frac{4 x}{5},\\quad y(0)=-6\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{5}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{4 x}{5}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\frac{x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{5}y) & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\cdot \\frac{4 x}{5} \\\\ e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5}y & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}) & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{x^{2}}{10}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}} & =\\int 4e^u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}} & =4e^u+C \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}} & =4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{10}})+C}{(e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{10}})} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - 10 e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{10}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2f7cde-9fc6-5255-af89-803232279137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495415} {:answer/id #uuid "9b0d71a0-6b12-555c-acf5-0e607f6a8f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- \\frac{x^{3}}{9}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495451} {:answer/id #uuid "a618af7d-df0c-5ffb-8cfb-545b9c46c80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{2 x^{3}}{9}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495454} {:answer/id #uuid "cf44d531-e321-505a-a3b0-d6280d41958b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e2f7cde-9fc6-5255-af89-803232279137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495415} :answer-field/id #uuid "0002121f-fc27-5505-8379-9be6d5c531ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310f4b13-ac78-5765-a4a