P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x^{2}}{3}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{5 x^{2}}{3}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\frac{x^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x^{2}}{3}y) & =e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}\\cdot \\frac{5 x^{2}}{3} \\\\ e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x^{2} e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}}{3}y & =\\frac{5 x^{2} e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}) & =\\frac{5 x^{2} e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{x^{3}}{9}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{5 x^{2} e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}} & =\\int 5e^u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}} & =5e^u+C \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}} & =5 e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 5 e^{\\frac{x^{3}}{9}}\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{3}}{9}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(5 e^{\\frac{(0)^{3}}{9}})+C}{(e^{\\frac{(0)^{3}}{9}})} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{5+C}{1} \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5 + e^{- \\frac{x^{3}}{9}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c39dc7b-1910-5aa2-b559-13bc4f97e9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 9 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495389} {:answer/id #uuid "42b1d7a7-d499-5