5407} {:answer/id #uuid "620022f9-c82b-5c21-a4bf-b021e0a54ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495425} {:answer/id #uuid "69d4960a-7b0d-5fb9-a902-9c6541e69089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{12 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c5042ce-f847-5c29-9acf-80f90e962e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495390} :answer-field/id #uuid "987bb710-d32e-5715-b02d-a9923b5a5d2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "43867ed7-bd35-5123-ad3b-db1c0f0e8adf" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(6\\right)y=6 x e^{- 6 x},\\quad y(0)=6\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=6$ and $Q(x)=6 x e^{- 6 x}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 6\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{6 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{6 x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{6 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y) & =e^{6 x}\\cdot 6 x e^{- 6 x} \\\\ e^{6 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6 e^{6 x}y & =6 x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{6 x}) & =6 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{6 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6 x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{6 x} & =3 x^{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 3 x^{2}\\right) e^{- 6 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(3 (0)^{2})+C}{(e^{6 (0)})} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{0+C}{1} \\\\ C & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=3 \\left(x^{2} + 2\\right) e^{- 6 x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08659bee-8d2e-5515-adac-a5ea49dd379a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495377} {:answer/id #uuid "76808c42-025e-5359-8d45-59a8789a18d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495434} {:answer/id #uuid "807d3623-3816-5512-b17f-f571616e79ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495440} {:answer/id #uuid "f50cd3e3-7ba6-5fff-b7c4-da949e5bffb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "807d3623-3816-5512-b17f-f571616e79ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495440} :answer-field/id #uuid "55504a9f-6299-5853-ac2f-dc92a45d58fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dac8a8c-2875-5a2f-bd58-637669580691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 x^{4} - 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495437} {:answer/id #uuid "86cf8a09-ce49-530f-9d22-d5c471375646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{12}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495443} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb441f6-0fd6-59dc-93f3-cbfe1de42881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x^{4} + 12}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495462} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6c0325-0d3a-59f5-bfc9-4676fb4655fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 \\left(x^{4} - 2\\right)}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495465} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec5df9-73ff-51e7-b62f-42505cb2e83a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 x^{2} - 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf6c0325-0d3a-59f5-bfc9-4676fb4655fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 \\left(x^{4} - 2\\right)}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495465} :answer-field/id #uuid "f365ea67-3727-58fc-9a9f-8975152e3264" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "440a15bb-8981-5d44-b0fa-73854b5eaffc" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=24 x^{2},\\quad x>0,\\quad y(1)=-6\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The first step is to write the equation in standard form,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y & =24 x^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}\\left(x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y\\right) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 24 x^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y & =24 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=24 x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\frac{2}{x}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}} \\\\  & =x^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=x^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & =x^{2}\\cdot 24 x \\\\ x^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 xy & =24 x^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx^{2}) & =24 x^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 24 x^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ yx^{2} & =6 x^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{C + 6 x^{4}}{x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =\\frac{(6 (1)^{4})+C}{((1)^{2})} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6 \\left(x^{4} - 2\\right)}{x^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2de88f-449d-540b-8b73-ee09ab14037c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495380} {:answer/id #uuid "10762d6d-5f37-53c0-b521-e9659ffcb04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495384} {:answer/id #uuid "1606c6b9-4509-53c6-9b3c-5ce2d6e88a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495388} {:answer/id #uuid "85ab0b88-f11d-5d78-83d3-d5b6663a6bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85ab0b88-f11d-5d78-83d3-d5b6663a6bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495442} :answer-field/id #uuid "3290d38e-24d0-5d5c-8b02-d6319bb5b746" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "136f8070-e038-59b5-9fae-cc4aac2ce567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} + 1\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495385} {:answer/id #uuid "4c99787c-3a80-51ac-89ed-ebbc62aa8a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495414} {:answer/id #uuid "777b2bb8-63c0-5f2f-8f20-40d85000e233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495435} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8f8405-7f27-5cdb-ad75-7a89cb48ea49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495439} {:answer/id #uuid "bef28809-b661-57e3-be19-5c756dbfb6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f8f8405-7f27-5cdb-ad75-7a89cb48ea49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495439} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2efdafc-989a-566c-b1bc-a7366ec9afa2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5638cec7-278c-5fc7-b8a9-e5331fdd2e7c" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)y=\\frac{4 x}{3},\\quad y(0)=3\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{3}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{4 x}{3}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\frac{x}{3}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{3}y) & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\cdot \\frac{4 x}{3} \\\\ e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3}y & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}) & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{x^{2}}{6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} & =\\int 4e^u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} & =4e^u+C \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} & =4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6}})+C}{(e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6}})} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e71318-5920-5caf-9325-80e6065404cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 e^{x} - 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495393} {:answer/id #uuid "49202a76-3117-5bcc-aa4c-6349fef0d506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 12 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495413} {:answer/id #uuid "549dac5b-a505-5710-9807-2c1d539e1b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495418} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0660cc-710f-5461-ba04-d387305d719e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 e^{x} + 12\\right) e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495436} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ba0ee9-9174-572a-a7ec-3f4e29eb93df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49202a76-3117-5bcc-aa4c-6349fef0d506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 12 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495413} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd7f627e-b82f-5a54-a107-26f3f06ce903" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "144d0822-f694-5e68-9bbf-5a7bcbcfeb5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495386} {:answer/id #uuid "2086f1a2-34d5-56df-8318-c4c682be406d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495391} {:answer/id #uuid "23ea1197-6f72-5d57-99d6-0cd13ade6fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495392} {:answer/id #uuid "57e80fab-97cd-5361-bb79-7f984ac78102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "144d0822-f694-5e68-9bbf-5a7bcbcfeb5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495386} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0243a87-1866-5a25-a8d1-d7d58740395d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5ed01c36-e086-5285-ba76-12d3ecc939c4" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(1\\right)y=6,\\quad y(0)=-6\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=6.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 6 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =6 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =6 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =6\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =6 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 6 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(6 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6 - 12 e^{- x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28742a9d-d802-59d5-837f-4c7ae6647c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 10 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495394} {:answer/id #uuid "50a716cc-eef7-580a-b2ed-f4f20c746b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 e^{x} + 10\\right) e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495416} {:answer/id #uuid "6203d589-0980-5569-95ab-ec6b00d190e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 e^{x} - 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495426} {:answer/id #uuid "90fcb6b2-2e26-5cc7-a616-6ff510c06c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495445} {:answer/id #uuid "95ee8c84-645f-50cc-ae00-61b9756dbf67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 10 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ee8c84-645f-50cc-ae00-61b9756dbf67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/