ial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(1\\right)y=5,\\quad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=5.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 5 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =5 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =5 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =5\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =5 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 5 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(5 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{5+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5 - 6 e^{- x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e86e3f8-835a-5e7b-800f-ceabc4489397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577958} {:answer/id #uuid "3120bb10-b47c-5419-8adb-97f2655124d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577959} {:answer/id #uuid "a1417d20-4b8d-5020-96a5-2fbfbd7050c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577987} {:answer/id #uuid "b83df480-6b6b-5335-b4e1-f7290ebda4f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1417d20-4b8d-5020-96a5-2fbfbd7050c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577987} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab4e553-4d18-5597-a3e0-73deea59b791" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3570ef95-2759-5e30-953f-28e1ebb98a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{3 x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577960} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfccc74-2fa7-5b51-a206-88395113b5cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{6 x}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577968} {:answer/id #uuid "7331aa7a-74a0-5dd6-9a77-f5c139e3cdc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{6 x}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577975} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb021b5-ba70-5bfd-8dc9-a93c7df005cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{3 x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb021b5-ba70-5bfd-8dc9-a93c7df005cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{3 x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577984} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc886d9b-0870-5428-8a5d-36eef483e7f9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "16f4ba5c-38ec-56ab-af32-6a47ecbd1681" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{3}{x}y = 6, x > 0$.\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=6.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\ {x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}y & =6{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{3})\\,dx & =\\int 6{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =\\frac{6{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12ff3b91-e441-53af-9062-6172c2b943f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577952} {:answer/id #uuid "373e6e78-bb4e-5bed-a8e8-55dacc8ccc10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577961} {:answer/id #uuid "73