{x^{6}} + \\frac{e^{3 x}}{3 x^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577985} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b59f443-9037-5baa-accb-c0e1753df732" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f95006c4-b3c1-5054-956d-113fccb90ca1" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{{x}^{6}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{6}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{{x}^{6}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (6/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{6})} \\\\  & ={x}^{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{6}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}y) & ={x}^{6}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{{x}^{6}} \\\\ {x}^{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6{x}^{5}\\cdot y & ={e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{6})\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}+C}{{x}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cdbbe3c-eec3-59a6-b054-5cec462a5469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671088} {:answer/id #uuid "41263caa-37d4-5894-bdd4-055b030643a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671091} {:answer/id #uuid "5125e6f5-42dc-5d2b-ac35-771aef6e14de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{4 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{4 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671095} {:answer/id #uuid "ec3dff48-bdbc-5185-83e9-3143d4a0ffcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{7 x}{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{7 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671113} {:answer/id #uuid "f996046c-a5c8-5720-b5e3-35170c7906ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cdbbe3c-eec3-59a6-b054-5cec462a5469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671088} :answer-field/id #uuid "73c95eb2-c30a-586d-8c98-83cb726f1e9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "03037866-9e99-5a94-acdf-a5e7b89db4df" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)\\cdot y=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\n$$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{10}{3}$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{\\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671086 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49b9dacc-5eb7-5601-a991-c899cddfdc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671094} {:answer/id #uuid "5715b197-fea3-5795-a30f-eca5473766a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{10 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671096} {:answer/id #uuid "5eebc27c-cc1e-5d1d-8990-81b437046835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 4 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 4 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671098} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfe767a-bded-5152-80e4-58685e889a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{11 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{11 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671104} {:answer/id #uuid "970cbe8b-8d43-55ff-96af-cf74e39c9fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49b9dacc-5eb7-5601-a991-c899cddfdc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671094} :answer-field/id #uuid "65396b0d-596d-5a6b-b4ce-8766a7d89e23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1c8efe23-e1fe-5151-83ef-1ed23bccc20c" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(x\\right)\\cdot y=x^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor.\n\nAssume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-1$ and $Q(x)=x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(-1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e46a24-4c00-5189-98d7-bfa6a2a5cc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{3 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671082} {:answer/id #uuid "149a4b2e-3fbe-5e93-835e-fa11562b9a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671085} {:answer/id #uuid "47c71a09-eb51-5016-8a2d-b7f286957a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{\\frac{11 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{\\frac{11 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671093} {:answer/id #uuid "e77f6ee4-c86c-5466-bba9-ae18e96875b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671111} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9a849b-b505-51e2-9d27-afd52c0e2f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "149a4b2e-3fbe-5e93-835e-fa11562b9a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671085} :answer-field/id #uuid "b76c9b72-cfa7-545f-8b6a-053f48007a90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "34ac2e02-a12f-5cc4-8239-e8e5387b0f1f" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\n$$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=- \\frac{5}{2}$ and $Q(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04bd9421-b85f-5ced-83ce-bd91ecae0cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 e^{- x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671083} {:answer/id #uuid "5849bb21-c3c8-5362-8214-bedc3448cb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{3}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- \\frac{5 x}{3}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 e^{- x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671097} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd99f05-2c47-53ab-9a18-e401392146dd" :answer/