ield-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=16.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{4 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{4 x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{4 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & =e^{4 x}\\cdot 16 \\\\ e^{4 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4 e^{4 x}y & =16 e^{4 x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{4 x}) & =16 e^{4 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{4 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 16 e^{4 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{4 x} & =16\\left(\\frac{1}{4} e^{4 x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{4 x} & =4 e^{4 x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{4 x}\\right) e^{- 4 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{4 (0)})+C}{(e^{4 (0)})} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - 5 e^{- 4 x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a1e929-4a96-5b6d-b801-5e7a868c5754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671121} {:answer/id #uuid "14101e14-8be8-5a83-8159-4b120f92de63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671122} {:answer/id #uuid "3071ecc1-e64e-5cac-a471-3ca89216c63b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - e^{- 5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671128} {:an