b-20b5-5027-bc63-b2ab1dca5b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671147} :answer-field/id #uuid "926f24ce-5a73-57d8-ba32-8bac04a8abe5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dcf5ddd4-bac2-5722-b4c3-fac589abf42a" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(3\\right)y=18,\\quad y(0)=4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3$ and $Q(x)=18.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{3 x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{3 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y) & =e^{3 x}\\cdot 18 \\\\ e^{3 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3 e^{3 x}y & =18 e^{3 x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{3 x}) & =18 e^{3 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{3 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18 e^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{3 x} & =18\\left(\\frac{1}{3} e^{3 x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{3 x} & =6 e^{3 x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 6 e^{3 x}\\right) e^{- 3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(6 e^{3 (0)})+C}{(e^{3 (0)})} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6 - 2 e^{- 3 x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71eae54a-d93d-5657-ba12-81d85ed6cb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 + 2 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671146} {:answer/id #uuid "8822c766-03e4-5ba0-85d8-a63cdcfbd8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 2 e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671152} {:answer/id #uuid "abc4e823-c280-5bbf-9676-8363643a0c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 2 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671158} {:answer/id #uuid "ae346266-244d-53af-9983-43e97f10dc99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 + 2 e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671159} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d1d641-b783-502e-aea7-744475d60287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 - 3 e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abc4e823-c280-5bbf-9676-8363643a0c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 - 2 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671158} :answer-field/id #uuid "60869067-bdb9-56bd-abd1-bfcc72bc3b92" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671142} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83d05d53-ffca-595b-bb52-ff5d5b9978a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671150} {:answer/id #uuid "c39a0f66-0147-59d1-bd54-e4e65a527a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 175