e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =6\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =6 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 6 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(6 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6 - 2 e^{- x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032e85a2-ca00-5717-8bf7-636097e4e9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x}{x^2}+\\frac{\\cos x}{x}+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686234} {:answer/id #uuid "60b266fc-2e47-57b7-bc89-862f2ca01f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}-\\frac{\\cos x}{x^2}+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686246} {:answer/id #uuid "9a8ebfc9-e367-5ac0-91d2-44a7e9d434e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}+\\frac{\\cos x}{x^2}+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686257} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf9ca11-b5e4-5a5a-8926-156c28ed36b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}+\\frac{\\cos x}{x^2}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a8ebfc9-e367-5ac0-91d2-44a7e9d434e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x}{x}+\\frac{\\cos x}{x^2}+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686257} :answer-field/id #uuid "685d144a-fc90-5aef-a5aa-20605a71e0c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d8122f-7cfe-5212-a88a-dc48a1a9ed9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686235} {:answer/id #uuid "129b82ca-e221-5f23-a32e-65d350f56d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686237} {:answer/id #uuid "561b048f-f610-5093-8bc2-495a75db6a9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686245} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ce27f8-f565-5424-9360-68e1ac022c6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d8122f-7cfe-5212-a88a-dc48a1a9ed9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686235} :answer-field/id #uuid "81e9e5bf-90c8-5783-8794-22f246cf1601" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2dd91870-eedb-59ea-972d-2729a23d235b" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y=\\frac{\\cos x}{x},\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The equation is in standard form $y'+P(x)y=Q(x)$ with $P(x)=2/x$ and $Q(x)=\\cos x/x$. Since $x>0$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=e^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2\\ln x}=x^2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying by $x^2$ and using the product rule gives\n\n$$\nx^2y'+2xy=x\\cos x,\n\\qquad\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x^2y)=x\\cos x.\n$$\n\nHence $x^2y=\\int x\\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$. Evaluate this integral by parts using $u=x$, $\\mathrm{d}v=\\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, $\\mathrm{d}u=\\mathrm{d}x$, and $v=\\sin x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int x\\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=x\\sin x-\\int\\sin x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\n&=x\\sin x+\\cos x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after dividing every term by $x^2$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2y&=x\\sin x+\\cos x+C,\\\\\ny&=\\frac{\\sin x}{x}+\\frac{\\cos x}{x^2}+\\frac{C}{x^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b670f6-4107-5ec5-bc7d-3a5f3a1b9ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^3e^{2x}}{3}+Ce^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686240} {:answer/id #uuid "635a41b5-fe89-5157-acf3-620e8d969ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^3e^{2x}}{3}+Ce^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686248} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf127c2-6b06-56dc-af55-f8d8413cc7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2e^{-2x}}{3}+Ce^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686252} {:answer/id #uuid "b2034220-83af-5575-a942-4bc4ac54ca94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2e^{-2x}}{3}+Ce^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "635a41b5-fe89-5157-acf3-620e8d969ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^3e^{2x}}{3}+Ce^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686248} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f6f5ea-6b3b-5aed-a24f-ead5fc8584e1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f098680-ad5f-5d16-afe2-6943ddd86f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686242} {:answer/id #uuid "423fdc87-4716-5207-8ffa-5ba44e4fe7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686243} {:answer/id #uuid "65f098ca-be35-53b0-9db9-1fd5f897a3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686249} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a91413-0f87-5670-a9e9-1e90940b0061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2a91413-0f87-5670-a9e9-1e90940b0061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686265} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bff1f44-3a05-50ef-835b-bd74fcd54500" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae388928-c1e1-5718-873d-6d31403f9c0c" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}-2y=x^2e^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The equation is in standard form $y'+P(x)y=Q(x)$ with $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)=x^2e^{2x}$. Thus an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=e^{\\int -2\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the equation by $e^{-2x}$ gives\n\n$$\ne^{-2x}y'-2e^{-2x}y=x^2.\n$$\n\nThe left side is the derivative of $ye^{-2x}$ by the product rule. Integrating both sides and then dividing by the integrating factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(ye^{-2x})&=x^2,\\\\\nye^{-2x}&=\\frac{x^3}{3}+C,\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x^3e^{2x}}{3}+Ce^{2x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cce9bb7-60f8-5a4c-9ed1-452e5c42620f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686236} {:answer/id #uuid "848404ad-cd6c-531b-8fd4-f8bfe017bfde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686255} {:answer/id #uuid "99a0613e-96b6-521f-81a3-7c84bcd54675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686256} {:answer/id #uuid "a06608e7-45ec-5709-80d5-b65837daf063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cce9bb7-60f8-5a4c-9ed1-452e5c42620f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686236} :answer-field/id #uuid "632270d3-1192-585d-8fc7-19ce30f3e466" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b426c64-07e5-555e-bf84-d365ef0bbaf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686238} {:answer/id #uuid "3c811484-fc01-5d1e-b166-ebdce43168bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686241} {:answer/id #uuid "80464036-f947-57a0-b335-93cdf49391fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686253} {:answer/id #uuid "ab778aa5-02a2-5816-a087-f0586141ae36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab778aa5-02a2-5816-a087-f0586141ae36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686259} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42badc8-ec94-5230-8095-34d186226ea0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e60e1d8a-866c-56de-bb0f-bb9da5584bd9" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y=3,\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The equation is in standard form $y'+P(x)y=Q(x)$ with $P(x)=2/x$ and $Q(x)=3$. Since $x>0$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=e^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2\\ln x}=x^2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the equation by $x^2$ gives\n\n$$\nx^2y'+2xy=3x^2.\n$$\n\nBy the product rule the left side is the derivative of $x^2y$. Integrating and then dividing by $x^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x^2y)&=3x^2,\\\\\nx^2y&=x^3+C,\\\\\ny&=x+\\frac{C}{x^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entire expression, including the arbitrary constant, must be divided by $x^2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2276d439-9cb9-53b8-809a-6fd344a0816e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- 4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686837} {:answer/id #uuid "2e21d83c-b4cc-5a68-b1c4-df0a2431764b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686838} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8d06e0-0834-5251-b598-a25e5ca20675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686866} {:answer/id #uuid "fbff57ad-dbc4-59f6-bce9-26e804fc5f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbff57ad-dbc4-59f6-bce9-26e804fc5f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686884} :answer-field/id #uuid "75392269-1fdb-5f33-8c92-d28969674212" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820fbab6-ba62-55bb-ae40-0b1d5d2da8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C e^{- 3 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{- 3 x}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686859} {:answer/id #uuid "995e547a-5969-50b0-891e-a498c048d828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C e^{- 3 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{- 3 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686865} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ddf1a2-698c-5377-9f66-90a1ec0e6662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C e^{- 4 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{- 3 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686872} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bb78e3-3354-5ac6-a7f5-83b9a302cb08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C e^{- 4 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{- 3 x}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "995e547a-5969-50b0-891e-a498c048d828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C e^{- 3 x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{- 3 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686865} :answer-field/id #uuid "f357fe12-d174-5ad4-8083-487bd5c49b37" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0568e66f-449a-5e4c-b273-b7f6fb03b993" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y=x{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=3$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{-3x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y) & ={e}^{3x}\\cdot x{e}^{-3x} \\\\ {e}^{3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{e}^{3x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{3x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{3x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67407bcb-72ad-565f-a66a-d7e08a2b703e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- 3 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686848} {:answer/id #uuid "703ecbf7-ee1b-51b5-954b-800cc4eb5a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} 