/ref 17592186686840} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5777872-84e3-571e-82df-591e863a8e53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c6838d41-79ed-577b-b029-04635eb70b8a" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} - 2y = x^{1}e^{2x}$.\nSelect the correct options below.\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{2x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -2\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot x{e}^{2x} \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-2x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}}{2}+C{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e4d5f2b-f338-5b67-b124-87b4ada135af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686851} {:answer/id #uuid "9654245b-5efb-56c9-9288-399b465ce8fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498