/id #edb/ref 17592186686867} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6ba6171-118c-53ae-bfcc-388fda47b3be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f225644b-2ce4-5654-b784-6bf3e8f63023" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y={x}^{2}{e}^{-6x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=6$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{-6x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 6\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{6x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y) & ={e}^{6x}\\cdot {x}^{2}{e}^{-6x} \\\\ {e}^{6x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6{e}^{6x}\\cdot y & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{6x}) & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{6x})\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{6x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{e}^{-6x}}{3}+C{e}^{-6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f1c2a3-db4b-5e3c-a957-39376bcf5176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{6}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686888} {:answer/id #uuid "173a2053-feea-50ed-b54b-fb4a115de657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{5}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686889} {:answer/id #uuid "435602a1-f4d4-5640-b735-b02d7581f53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{5}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686898} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b51c81-e1c5-5a65-a84e-ea4b4174848d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{6}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "173a2053-feea-50ed-b54b-fb4a115de657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{5}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686889} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e6cb488-05bf-5f65-9940-e6b3fef20d70" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1754e527-9ee0-54f1-989b-204265d7f297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686890} {:answer/id #uuid "c32aa6a2-56d7-5222-bc0d-9a5747e5c3f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686921} {:answer/id #uuid "d01f4562-1677-5049-928d-c6d0a89f9742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686924} {:answer/id #uuid "db164594-21e9-558d-8c08-d4f86f19e406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db164594-21e9-558d-8c08-d4f86f19e406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686927} :answer-field/id #uuid "963764c0-9a07-5f11-bb6d-8d041781ec67" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "18a9fd9d-430c-577b-abda-f26c7a09fc10" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{4}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{5}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{4}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (5/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{5}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y) & ={x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {x}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{x}^{4}y & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{5}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{5})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ and $v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{5} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =x(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =x(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{4}\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}}}{4}-\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{4}}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52a7f4fa-60da-5a4c-aa9f-6f10e93bfedb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{2}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686903} {:answer/id #uuid "60d2aea3-0080-515e-af29-9a16cd13adb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{2}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686904} {:answer/id #uuid "69aea9eb-7b8f-51da-b078-3bf9e1873fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{2}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686907} {:answer/id #uuid "d1526efd-e3da-5cde-9dd0-1c9d776c6620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{2}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60d2aea3-0080-515e-af29-9a16cd13adb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{2}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686904} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eba6452-d82f-5730-84ce-8ddb734bc242" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50d148b8-fc5f-5720-9164-e27a609c842b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686902} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd62529-fc77-5eb6-80bb-9c681679c00f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686911} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6e57fb-9769-573b-90e0-4782b82812db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686916} {:answer/id #uuid "ae126d35-3059-5e34-8e58-3f5ccfd82e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fd62529-fc77-5eb6-80bb-9c681679c00f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686911} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90e9665-8beb-5610-8e08-e7ec81dfd5bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "261ce395-50e9-5626-b7c9-37d75332ec4e" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{2}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{2}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}y & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{3}) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{3})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ and $v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{3} & =\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2})-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{4}\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{3}}}{4}+\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{2}}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79ea2e72-b64b-50cc-af67-0648c20f1f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686909} {:answer/id #uuid "8290a9f4-f2fe-5e77-9534-d7f872413b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686913} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ae3206-0779-5780-a7bf-218e90f1fc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686923} {:answer/id #uuid "d2edb5ac-4cfe-5370-86a7-dc8f622c185a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2edb5ac-4cfe-5370-86a7-dc8f622c185a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686926} :answer-field/id #uuid "716f9894-975a-528c-8e46-1217b4b55774" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba6de06-2dfe-57c4-a02f-47c1431afdb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{7}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{5}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686895} {:answer/id #uuid "47e7ee98-4fd6-5881-80b3-7d8367297b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{7}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{5}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686900} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbfe33f-7010-5472-8ded-4d0805650d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{6}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{5}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686901} {:answer/id #uuid "c036ccc6-7a62-5d7f-b544-79077777e528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{6}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{5}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbfe33f-7010-5472-8ded-4d0805650d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{6}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2 x^{5}} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 x^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686901} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b33cbf-5490-5b67-8d17-1ffe98a6f454" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "41505508-d6d4-56d2-a9f0-ff1faa10a5d3" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{6}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (6/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{6}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{6}{x}y) & ={x}^{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}} \\\\ {x}^{6}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6{x}^{5}y & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{6}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{6})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ and $v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{6} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =x(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =x(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2})+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{6} & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{4}\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{{x}^{6}}}{4}-\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{x}^{5}}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f44c0f8-eda9-5e3a-9308-7411cb897eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{2}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686894} {:answer/id #uuid "669df105-ee50-53a8-9f5c-7745ac2d7a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686905} {:answer/id #uuid "81aaf3ce-14eb-5008-b351-0acf03c47c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686912} {:answer/id #uuid "f5207761-44e1-5cd5-bf76-34cb3ff29a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{2}} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f44c0f8-eda9-5e3a-9308-7411cb897eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{2}} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686894} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf61b42-0bf9-5826-ba88-f8754e768db8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686910} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66e94558-d571-5150-8309-21392b5e3da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686906} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9c2e4-0421-5cc7-a9a4-af883eae0b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686917} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ac1969-a416-50da-bcdc-ea4f7dab2101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686928} {:answer/id #uuid "f136fec3-6dff-5cd1-a48f-f8e8c99bbba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66e94558-d571-5150-8309-21392b5e3da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686906} :answer-field/id #uuid "941e3ded-a58f-5b6a-a18c-5a1b6bbcc5d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46fe9692-f8d8-53b2-a423-94b001901cd7" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a560d92-2b61-56bd-a9d6-3cff675eaed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{-2x}\\right)=e^{-2x}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686933} {:answer/id #uuid "31c6cfd6-df70-5cb4-a898-d33b9a2fbcda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{-2x}\\right)=\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686935} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1eaff0-bdf4-579d-99d9-1abb663edabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{2x}\\right)=e^{2x}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686936} {:answer/id #uuid "762778bf-c73e-59f0-971c-caeee888a9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y(-2x)\\right)=-2x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686938} {:answer/id #uuid "95262852-4a6b-59ca-bbf9-9878508f8c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{-2}\\right)=e^{-2}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a560d92-2b61-56bd-a9d6-3cff675eaed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{-2x}\\right)=e^{-2x}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686933} :answer-field/id #uuid "a35da2d2-c05b-5301-9976-a4343049f4d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7e8eecb8-13da-5d93-932d-9d047c834607" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-2y=\\sin x\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "The equation is already in standard form $y'+P(x)y=Q(x)$, with $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)=\\sin x$. An integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=e^{\\int -2\\,dx}=e^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying every term by $e^{-2x}$ gives\n\n$$\ne^{-2x}\\frac{dy}{dx}-2e^{-2x}y=e^{-2x}\\sin x.\n$$\n\nBy the product rule, the left side is $\\frac{d}{dx}(ye^{-2x})$. Thus the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{-2x}\\right)=e^{-2x}\\sin x.\n$$\n\nThe negative sign in $P(x)$ remains in the exponent. The right side must also be multiplied by the integrating factor."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5a0be8-cb00-578d-924a-41eae4ecc4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yx\\right)=\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686934} {:answer/id #uuid "8541e019-467c-5219-8b12-4455a24ad508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^{-x}\\right)=\\frac{e^{-x}\\cos x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686941} {:answer/id #uuid "88614a9b-e9dc-5d55-b88c-c7364c50c24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yxe^{-x}\\right)=xe^{-x}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686942} {:answer/id #uuid "d25b8de5-c14c-5e8a-a0b1-5e6a9f0e5dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yxe^{-x}\\right)=e^{-x}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686951} {:answer/id #uuid "f831fec6-2e42-538a-8169-f2de91313211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yxe^x\\right)=e^x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25b8de5-c14c-5e8a-a0b1-5e6a9f0e5dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yxe^{-x}\\right)=e^{-x}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686951} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a4018f9-bf62-533a-9572-6f5bc38a1084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc856375-23d5-56d2-8eb2-c51bf4a8076c" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x)$:\n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=xy+\\cos x,\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "Collect the $y$-terms on the left, then divide every term by $x>0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+(1-x)y&=\\cos x\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(\\frac{1}{x}-1\\right)y&=\\frac{\\cos x}{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $P(x)=1/x-1$ and $Q(x)=\\cos x/x$. Integrate both terms of $P(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI(x)&=e^{\\int (1/x-1)\\,dx}\\\\\n&=e^{\\ln x-x}\\\\\n&=xe^{-x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the standard-form equation by $xe^{-x}$:\n\n$$\nxe^{-x}\\frac{dy}{dx}+(1-x)e^{-x}y=e^{-x}\\cos x.\n$$\n\nSince $(xe^{-x})'=(1-x)e^{-x}$, the left side is the derivative of $yxe^{-x}$. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yxe^{-x}\\right)=e^{-x}\\cos x.\n$$\n\nBoth collecting the $y$-terms and dividing the right side by $x$ are needed before applying the integrating factor."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186686950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07709b3a-2501-5565-81c4-b42c41c97f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\ln x\\right)=(\\ln x)\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686932} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7aaf64-8ba0-517a-9c82-2584a3a45565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yx^2\\right)=x^2\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686939} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9ae577-3524-54cb-a6c3-3cc0a08672c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)=\\frac{\\sin x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686944} {:answer/id #uuid "98e03d92-5091-5f63-954f-216339641586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yx\\right)=x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686946} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9c0623-de66-57ea-98a4-67acbeea7f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(ye^x\\right)=e^x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98e03d92-5091-5f63-954f-216339641586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(yx\\right)=x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686946} :answer-field/id #uuid "88834d2a-19b0-5300-b83b-719161181b49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186686943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cedf21ff-9f0a-58db-b3ad-dacaa099c7e6" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x)$:\n\n$$\nx^2\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy=x^2\\sin x,\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First divide every term by $x^2$, which is nonzero on $x>0$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}y=\\sin x.\n$$\n\nNow $P(x)=1/x$ and $Q(x)=\\sin x$. Since $x>0$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=e^{\\int (1/x)\\,dx}=e^{\\ln x}=x.\n$$\n\nMultiply the standard-form equation by $x$:\n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x\\sin x.\n$$\n\nThe product rule gives $\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=xy'+y$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\sin x.\n$$\n\nThe integrating factor comes from the coefficient $1/x$ after normalization, rather than the coefficient $x$ in the original equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16aeac5c-b620-5c9d-9dcf-e072b7369aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687314} {:answer/id #uuid "6844ca24-1940-53dc-93ff-e37d27a1ebd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687316} {:answer/id #uuid "abc07162-c8c0-5854-b2b9-b3c4067ebd19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{4}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687317} {:answer/id #uuid "b12bd4a1-17e7-5f92-a7b2-fddfaeba76c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687318} {:answer/id #uuid "c3627b40-a4fc-509f-878d-b291a52c8cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b12bd4a1-17e7-5f92-a7b2-fddfaeba76c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687318} :answer-field/id #uuid "b84938bc-a847-594c-bdfc-0ded1214f504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2bd9adcb-43c8-511a-8269-f9dc21b93e60" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-y=-1\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor.\n\nAssume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot y=- \\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=- \\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=- \\frac{1}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =I(x)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\ I(x)\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)I(x)y & =\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
